+/// destination in the r/m field, so the byte is `0xC0 | reg` (NOT
+/// `0xC0 | (reg << 3)` — that would select the undefined `C7 /reg` form
+/// and #UD on every register except %eax, where the two fields happen
+/// to coincide).
